{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Your wife like a fruitful vine</b> — that she give birth in her time. The meaning: every vine is outside the house, exposed to the sun; therefore he said, round about. <b>Like olive saplings</b> — in their strength, and the leaves of the olive tree shall not wither."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 128, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:22.860683858Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}